  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Genomics and Science Dojo: Accelerating Outputs and Action 2.0 and UK-Indonesia Genomic Forum 2025</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Genomics and Science Dojo 2.0 aims to build on the Dojo 1.0 to further enhance biomedical science and genomic analysis skills for improved decision-making, dissemination and publication. Capacity for genomic data analysis and inference is crucial to provide evidence-based policy for use of genomics to promote health and development.

The outcomes will be indicated from the following: 
(1)	Improvement in technical skills of researchers and academia on genomics data analysis. This will be measured by the proportion of participants with an improvement of knowledge by 80%.
(2)	Improvement in soft skills of researchers and academia to showcase the genomics analysis results through written or verbal format. This will be indicated by the number of publications/knowledge products resulting from this project and qualified to be published or showcase/presented at a scientific conference or wider audience.
(3)	Enhancement genomics dojo implementation for wider audience. The curriculum and workbook will be made available for a wider user and scale up. The number of participants from clinicians (externals/visitors) will also be measured to assess the success.

The UK-Indonesia Genomic Forum aims to build capacity, strengthen UK-Indonesia partnerships in health genomics, supporting policy development, research, and industry collaborations that benefits populations in both the UK and Indonesia, and accelerating research, innovation, and translation into public health improvements. The Forum aligns with the Dojo target and will help to connect the Dojo participant with the UK stakeholders in the Forum.</narrative>
  </description>
